    "body": "Not new in this PR, but I feel the behavior is slightly under-defined here: the text ignores the case of resources that do not have a single origin. For example, an svg image may indirectly include cross-origin content via foreignObject tag. It is obvious that tainting is the right thing to do when there are multiple origins, but being clearer about this in the spec would help prevent occasional confusion. In the past, I have fielded reports from web devs where they believed the tainting was non-compliant. Care to do a drive-by fix for that? I don't feel strongly about this, so I'll leave it up to your judgement. I just felt it was worth mentioning.\n",
