    "body": "Blink and WebKit work like @annevk described in terms of disabling subresources. We share the same leaky `<foreignObject>` implementation and we do not trust that content in `<foreignObject>` is single-origin, so we taint the canvas for anything containing `<foreignObject>`. We do allow data urls which significantly complicates this overzealous tainting, but content from Adobe Illustrator depends on this.\n\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=294129#c21 has more information about why `<foreignObject>` is leaky. I think there's a reasonable path forward for both engines to match the spec, just need to work through some security details.\n",
    "created_at": "2016-03-23T20:24:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-24T08:26:01Z",
